socrates: the ABL-handoff dance - fDeviceInit, then SSU POWER_CONDITION=ACTIVE

Flash #7 (Plan B): the ABL's handoff leaves the link UP (the ready gate
passes, no wake needed) but the device in needs-init state; TUR
CHECK-CONDITIONs (response 0x1, status 0x2) on every retry - the M2
first-flash behavior. The shim's v19 cure: SET fDeviceInit, poll until
the device clears it, retry TUR.

Flash #8/#9: the flag reads CLEAR (the ABL already ran bring-up) yet TUR
still refuses. Flash #10's sense named the disease: key 2 / ASC-ASCQ
04-02 - 'LOGICAL UNIT NOT READY, INITIALIZING COMMAND REQUIRED'. The
initializing command, panel-proven in the shim's M2 v18: START STOP UNIT
with POWER_CONDITION = ACTIVE (byte 4 = 0x11; the plain START_VALID form
draws 05/24 INVALID FIELD IN CDB). Then TUR once more.

The chain lives in its own blocks between the first TUR loop and the
partition lookup; the 00xx patches own that function's interior, so this
rides after the series instead of editing 0028 (whose context 0030/0034
patch byte-for-byte).
